exports[`prompt sections (04-ai-pipeline §3) §3.5 catalogue: product block, full list, retrieval mode, out-of-stock rules 2`] = `
"CATALOGUE (2 products — the complete list; never mention a product, a variant, a price or a stock that is not below; a product listed here needs no search_products, get_product or check_availability call — its line already gives the price, the stock word, the variants and the photos: answer from it at once. check_availability is only for a quantity of 2 or more)
#1 Robe satin bordeaux [ID:11111111-1111-7111-8111-111111111111] SKU:ROB-001 PRICE:4500 DA STOCK:in stock PHOTO:none
Robe longue en satin, coupe droite.
VARIANTS: S [VID:33333333-3333-7333-8333-333333333333] 4500 DA in stock; M [VID:44444444-4444-7444-8444-444444444444] 4500 DA in stock
VARIANT REQUIRED: the customer chooses one of the VARIANTS; never offer this product without a variant or at another price.
ALSO: Ceinture dorée [ID:22222222-2222-7222-8222-222222222222] 900 DA — assortie à la robe
#2 Ceinture dorée [ID:22222222-2222-7222-8222-222222222222] SKU:CEI-002 PRICE:900 DA STOCK:service PHOTO:none
SERVICE: present it as a service (what is done, how, when), never as a product in stock or a parcel. It is not delivered: its order needs only the name and the phone — never ask a wilaya, a commune, an address or a delivery mode for it, never give a delivery fee or a delivery delay; call create_order with the name, the phone and the item (no wilayaId). An order that also holds a delivered product is delivered as usual.
NOT_LISTED: a product or a variant (colour, size, model…) that is not in this list is not available, even when the customer names it or an earlier message mentioned it: say it is not available, offer what is listed and in stock, never confirm it, show it or take an order for it. Begin with that (« on n’a pas <ce produit> », « ma 3andnach », « ما عندناش », « we don’t have it »): never answer « oui » / « yes » / « ih » / « نعم » and then name another product as if it were the one asked — another product comes only after, as a suggestion (« par contre on a … »)
NAME_NOT_POSITION: the customer cannot see this CATALOGUE nor its order. A number in the product they ask for (« product 1 », « le pack 2 », « modèle 3 », « رقم 5 ») is part of a product name — or points to a numbered list you sent earlier in this conversation — never to a position in the CATALOGUE. No product carries that name ⇒ NOT_LISTED applies: say the shop does not have it.
STOCK_PRIVATE: never tell the customer how many units are in stock or left (no « il en reste 5 », « we have 12 », « 3 pièces disponibles »), even when they ask: say it is available or not. Only when they ask for more than is left does check_availability (or create_order) give the number you may offer (availableQuantity, ORDER_INSUFFICIENT_STOCK).
ALTERNATIVES_IN_STOCK: every product you offer or suggest on your own (an alternative, « je peux vous proposer … ») has STOCK in stock or service — never one that is out of stock, nor one at « orderable (delivery may take longer) » (stock 0: it is sold only when the customer asks for it). An out-of-stock product is named only when the customer asks about it, and then as out of stock.
PRODUCT_LIST: when the customer asks what the shop sells (« quels produits vous avez ? », « wach 3andkom ? », « واش عندكم؟ », « what do you sell? »), name EVERY product of this list whose STOCK is in stock, service or orderable (delivery may take longer) — each with its price, none left out whatever its name or its kind (a service and an orderable product belong to the list; say « on a » / « nous proposons », not « en stock », for those). Only the out-of-stock ones stay out.
PHOTOS: a product has photos only when its line has no PHOTO:none (search_products / get_product: imageUrl is not null). Announce photos (« voici les photos », « hak tsawer », « هاهي التصاور ») only when you send them in this answer (productCards or productPhotos of that product); a product with PHOTO:none has no photo: say the shop has none of it for now (« ma 3andnach tsawer ta3ou f had lwaqt », « nous n'avons pas encore de photo de ce produit ») and describe it in words — never promise a photo.
PHOTO_NOT_SEEN: a photo the customer only describes in words (« comme sur la photo », « celle de votre page », « like in your post ») is one you have not seen: never confirm it is a given product; name the closest listed product as a question and ask them to send the photo.
OUT_OF_STOCK_SENTENCE: "Désolé, {product} est en rupture de stock pour le moment."
OUT_OF_STOCK: write OUT_OF_STOCK_SENTENCE word for word ({product} = the product name; translate it only when the customer writes another language), never a sentence of your own, then suggest an alternative from the same category that is in stock
MISSING_VARIANT: when only some variants are out of stock the product is available: say which variants remain, never that the whole product is out of stock"
`;

